          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delhi_Sultanate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "phase": "khalji_expansion",
      "years": "1290–1320",
      "description": "Alauddin Khalji conquers most of India including Gujarat, Rajputana, and reaches south India; introduces price controls and market reforms; defeats multiple Mongol invasions including at Amroha (1305); empire reaches greatest territorial extent",
      "sources": [
        {
          "type": "wikidata",
          "id": "Q229411",
          "url": "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q229411"
        },
        {
          "type": "wikipedia",
          "label": "Delhi Sultanate",
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delhi_Sultanate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "phase": "tughluq_zenith_and_collapse",
      "years": "1320–1414",
      "description": "Muhammad bin Tughluq's ill-fated capital transfer to Daulatabad and currency reforms cause chaos; Ibn Battuta visits (1333–1342); Timur's devastating sack of Delhi (1398) ends Tughluq power; Sultanate shrinks to rump state",
      "sources": [
        {
          "type": "wikidata",
          "id": "Q229411",
          "url": "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q229411"
        },
        {
          "type": "wikipedia",
          "label": "Delhi Sultanate",
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delhi_Sultanate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "phase": "terminal_decline",
      "years": "1414–1526",
      "description": "Sayyid and Lodi dynasties rule a reduced Delhi Sultanate; Afghan Lodi dynasty briefly revives strength but Babur's Mughal army with artillery defeats Ibrahim Lodi at First Panipat (1526)",
      "sources": [
        {
          "type": "wikidata",
